I wrote [result-rogue_sneak_attack.json](/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/2751797-rogue_sneak_attack/result-rogue_sneak_attack.json) and [proposal-rogue_sneak_attack.md](/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/2751797-rogue_sneak_attack/proposal-rogue_sneak_attack.md). The proposal calls out the required gaps: a `class_feature.on_hit_trigger` family, eligibility predicates for the advantage/ally/no-disadvantage gate plus finesse-or-ranged weapon use, and a way to express damage type inherited from the weapon hit. I did not run `pnpm typecheck` or the tracer, because doing so would require a knowingly false placeholder encoding.
